From: NGM <ngm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ngm-compat: build ext/openssl against OpenSSL 3 (RSA_SSLV23_PADDING)

What: guard the OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING constant registration with
#ifdef RSA_SSLV23_PADDING, which OpenSSL 3.0 removed. Without it
ext/openssl does not compile against our private OpenSSL 3.5.

Why ours: CloudLinux ships this exact hunk for 5.6/7.x as
php-<ver>-fix-for-openssl-3.0.x.patch, but builds ea-php53 only on EL8
(OpenSSL 1.1), so the 5.3 series has no OpenSSL-3 follow-up to its
php-5.3.29-openssl11.patch (which we force-keep). The hunk is
byte-identical to CloudLinux's 5.6 one.

Behaviour change: on OpenSSL 3 the PHP constant OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING is
not defined (the padding mode no longer exists). Same as 5.6/7.x here.

Delete when: CloudLinux ships an OpenSSL-3 follow-up for ea-php53, or 5.3
is retired.
---
--- a/ext/openssl/openssl.c
+++ b/ext/openssl/openssl.c
@@ -1180,7 +1180,9 @@
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("PKCS7_NOSIGS", PKCS7_NOSIGS, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_PKCS1_PADDING", RSA_PKCS1_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
+#ifdef RSA_SSLV23_PADDING
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_SSLV23_PADDING", RSA_SSLV23_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
+#endif
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_NO_PADDING", RSA_NO_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 	REGISTER_LONG_CONSTANT("OPENSSL_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING", RSA_PKCS1_OAEP_PADDING, CONST_CS|CONST_PERSISTENT);
 
